  "result": "I reviewed the diff and found a material defect: the rewritten `last_n` (`items[len(items) - n:]`) breaks exactly the case the PR says it preserves.\n\n- **n > len(items)**: `len(items) - n` goes negative, so the slice starts near the *end* instead of clamping to the start (e.g. `[1,2,3]` with `n=5` \u2192 old returns `[1,2,3]`, new returns `[2,3]`). This directly contradicts the stated PR intent.\n- **n == 0**: old `items[-0:]` returns the whole list; new `items[len(items):]` returns `[]` \u2014 a silent regression.\n\nI wrote the review as `review-payload.json` (outcome: `findings`, one P0 must-fix item with a suggested fix \u2014 clamp with `max(0, len(items) - n)` \u2014 and a request for regression tests on `n=0` and `n > len(items)`).",
